      "writtenOn": "2025-03-13T01:36:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It shouldn\u0027t happen except in AOSP code, but if an OEM modified Wifi, then it\u0027s possible we get a WIFI_AP_STATE_CHANGE disabled event for an iface we\u0027ve never heard of.\n\nThe original code checked this in disableWifiIpServingCommon and logged an error if there was no TetherState found, but actually it continues to try to find a wifi TetherState in Pre-T. Thus I\u0027ve removed this null check and readded it back to disableWifiIpServingCommon. The null check isn\u0027t needed elsewhere since the other usages of ensureIpServerUnwanted already null-check the TetherState before calling into it.",
      "parentUuid": "88be7d8f_3c85bd69",
